# CODEOWNERS — Lumenpulse
#
# Owners are review *requests*, not merge rights. Being an owner means a change
# under your path needs your eyes before it lands; it does not mean you can merge
# it. Required approvals are configured as a branch protection rule, not here.
#
# Provenance: each area is mapped to the two contributors with the most merged
# pull requests touching that area on `main`. The mapping is a starting point,
# not a verdict — if you own something and the mapping is wrong, open a PR that
# fixes this file rather than working around it.
#
# ORDERING. GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so the catch-all `*` must
# come first; if it came last it would win against every specific rule below it
# and this file would do nothing. Specific rules follow, most general to most
# specific.
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners

# Catch-all: nothing is ever unowned, and scripts/check-codeowners.mjs reports
# any path that matches only this rule so the gap is visible rather than silent.
*                           @fadee26 @paris27-A

